blindly:
By rugged ways and thro' the night
We struggle blindly toward the light;
And groping, stumbling, ever pray

blinking:
And a shaking, sharp, suspicious way;
His blinking eyes had scarcely brooked
The light of day.

blistered:
It burned me in the night,
It blistered in my dream;
It sickened fresh upon my sight

bliss:
Who else had dared for thee what I have dared?
I plunged the depth most deep from bliss above;
I not My flesh, I not My spirit spared:

blinked:
Where the Babe sucked; or, Lamia in her first
Moonlighted pallor, ere she shrunk and blinked,
And, shuddering, wriggled down to the unclean;

blithely:
But his star was high, so he braved the main,
And sailed him blithely home again;
And with joy he bended his footsteps soon

blistering:
I laboured on alone. The wind and dust
And sun of the world beat blistering in my face;
